    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1119">

                <pb facs="1040" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/1678</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bernstorff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">J. Nr. B 2887]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 19, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 20</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: Referring to your
                    excellency’s kind note No. 1220 of the 3d instant,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1119-f1"/> I have the honor to inform your excellency that it has
                    been reported to me that 8 submarines are being built for Great Britain by the
                    Union Iron Works at San Francisco, and also 12 at Boston and Seattle, and that
                    they are to be forwarded piecemeal to England.</p>
                <p>Referring to my note of the 27th ultimo on the subject of the delivery of
                    submarines to Canada by the Bethlehem Steel Works, I have the, honor to ask of
                    your excellency a prompt investigation of the matter as it seems that the boats,
                    or at least a part of them, will be completed next week. I should be
                    particularly obliged to your excellency if you would most kindly apprise me of
                    the action that may have been taken in the case.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
